: 750406, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Twcg76bee8B34WThTmk2x5", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 756754, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own comment said it uses banker's rounding per FIN-212. The test expects 2.665 to round to 2.66, and `ROUND_HALF_UP` gives 2.67.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** The first run passed. When I tried to open the PR, it was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, checked the fix and test were still there, and re-ran CI. That run also passed.\n\nI couldn't check the fix against FIN-212 itself because the advisory lookup tool doesn't recognise that ID. I based the change on the test and the existing comment, and said so in the PR description. The PR hasn't been merged; that needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QPobqx8zEssfRg2ud3eiMy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01K6jc3tBk4DhZFGNtqK9t75", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NBFqGbcD19yy4Y4EqQkNCf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018sWxs1JDpMecPRsNzH7JGH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "ty